{"title":"1993 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f12ec5ee4a2e5304810da76fbb60e0d3cf46c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, determine, with proof, which of the two positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8cac81e3d9c2751d3306d933e8d4212fa64c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n = a + 1, \\quad b^{2n} = b + 3a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>is larger.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral such that diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at right angles, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be their intersection. Prove that the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b3ffdd33c14d94e964424e4a67cde5a8bbc486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : [0, 1] \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> which satisfy\n</p>\n<table><tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</td><td>(i)</td><td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0cd5dce73495458301961216e7272ef4ee67a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\ge0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab178d831a786b92cb4c9ddc2d33578223036f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />,</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</td><td>(ii)</td><td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dd0ff40babd7fbd0c3e3d3b019627c27949616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />,</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</td><td>(iii)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</td><td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b10eb6e96f1f642eb0f35e03ea62de2d074d89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) + f(y) \\le f(x + y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a859acebdd07c34704648be45c0daf108e2a29d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> are all in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab178d831a786b92cb4c9ddc2d33578223036f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Find, with proof, the smallest constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e93ec7efefb0af408a87d3d13e41a9e5bd902e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) \\le cx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>for every function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> satisfying (i)-(iii) and every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab178d831a786b92cb4c9ddc2d33578223036f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be odd positive integers. Define the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18c45a6f5594393fb69b334d085b975bf82736a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> by putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0655d6b0418915b20ddb8697b0ae7c44762229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f081c1a94710157491eb3d6757fbaa6bd76224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_2 = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" />, and by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b21b36bfc3bad4b81f5aed2c6f5613bc98403ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> be the greatest odd divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4b8fb965ef8bfa275a5543fc6096b365e4008c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n-1} + f_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />.\nShow that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is constant for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sufficiently large and determine the eventual\nvalue as a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a11edcbc60c4f62bae1924c7f12df4e9bf535b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, a_2,\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence of positive real numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f738c4009c0be32bacdc42ccd2d616207a334a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i-1}a_{i+1}\\le a^2_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/42796503a95813394ec9c1b4addc9fb6047b9655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2, 3,\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> . (Such a sequence is said to be <i>log concave</i>.) Show that for\neach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da21136d8f04ee35b3510f5fb8653b483dc8131b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_0+\\cdots+a_n}{n+1}\\cdot\\frac{a_1+\\cdots+a_{n-1}}{n-1}\\ge\\frac{a_0+\\cdots+a_{n-1}}{n}\\cdot\\frac{a_1+\\cdots+a_{n}}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"504\" height=\"37\" />.</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO\" title=\"1993 USAMO\">1993 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO\" title=\"1992 USAMO\">1992 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_USAMO\" title=\"1994 USAMO\">1994 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8073/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.455      1 -total\n 56.60%    7.049      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 40.98%    5.104      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8660:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043743 and revision id 79559. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}